meta {
  name: Reserve Stock
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/reserve
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "skuCode": "{{productId}}",
        "quantity": 1
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  In production this is only ever called service-to-service by order-service
  (InventoryClient.reserve, see order-service/Create Order.bru) — this request lets
  you exercise it directly, bypassing order-service entirely.

  Atomic per-item conditional decrement (InventoryRepository.decrement, a single
  UPDATE ... WHERE quantity >= ? per item, inside one @Transactional method) — if any
  item in the list can't be decremented, InsufficientStockException is thrown and the
  whole batch rolls back (nothing else in the same request is left partially applied).

  Through "Gateway" this needs ROLE_ADMIN: JwtAuthenticationFilter.requiresAdmin
  matches ANY POST under /api/inventory/**, not just the admin-facing insert/update
  endpoints — so /reserve and /release are gated the same as inventory management,
  even though they're really an internal order-service-to-inventory-service contract.
  Worth flagging as a design quirk, not a deliberate access-control decision. Through
  "InventoryDirect" no auth is checked at all either way.

  Expected: 204 No Content, or 409 CONFLICT if quantity exceeds what's in stock — see
  inventory-service-errors/Reserve Insufficient Stock.bru.
}
